 "text": "Christian County Missouri\nSkip to main content\nSkip to primary sidebar\nSearch this website\nChristian County Missouri\nHome\nAbout Us\nAbout Us\nCounty Statistics\nMaps to Locations\nVideo Tours\nHow Do I…\nApply For\nAbsentee Voting\nBuilding Permit\nFood Stamps\nJob\nMerchant’s License\nSpecial Event Permit Process\nWIC\nLicense & Permits\nPay Online\nChild Support\nCourt Costs/Filing Fees\nPersonal Property Tax\nReal Estate Tax\nRecords\nBirth Certificates\nMarriage Certificates\nProperty Tax Receipt\nReal Estate Receipt\nRegister As\nSex Offender\nVoter\nRegister My\nStorm Shelter\nPhone in Mass Notification System\nSpecial Needs Relative\nReport\nChild Abuse\nCrime\nCounty Road Issue\nDrug/Crime Tip Line\nContact Us\nMain Menu\nAssessor\nPublic GIS Viewer\nGIS Registration\nSenate Bill 190 Application\nPersonal Property Online Filing\nAuditor\nCollector\nCommission\n2020 Census: Christian County Counts\nPurchasing\nEmergency Management\nHighways & Roads\nHuman Resources\nEmployment Application & Opportunities\nEmployee of the Quarter\nEmployee Suggestion\nMeetings & Agendas\nAppointed Boards\nLibrary Board of Trustees\nCoroner\nCounty Clerk\nAbsentee Voting\nChange Name or Address\nElection Calendar\nElection Results\nMilitary & Overseas Voters\nPolling Locations\nSample Ballots\nCourts\nProsecutor\nPublic Administrator\nRecorder\nSheriff\nTreasurer\nPlanning & Development\nBuilding Regulations\nEnvironmental\nNational Flood Insurance\nRecycling\nPrevious\nNext\nElection Results\nSpecial Event Permit Process\nEmployment Opportunities\nPay Your Taxes Online\nFinancial Transparency\nC.E.R.T. Disaster Training\nHighways & Roads\nEmployee Health Clinic\nShop Where You Live\nEmployment Opportunities\nChristian County has a variety of employment opportunities throughout the year. Here is a list of the current ones.\nFind Out Now\nSB 190 – SENIOR CITIZEN REAL ESTATE TAX CREDIT\nRenewal for previously approved applicants will be automatic, so long as all eligibility\nrequirements are met (except for notarization), and no new improvements have been made\non the property. If a spouse has recently become age eligible, an application is required to\nadd them.\nFirst-time applications for the Senior Citizen Real Estate Tax Credit will be available March\n1, 2027, at the Collector’s Office. Completed applications will be accepted until June 15,\n2027 atthe Collector’s Office, Room 101, in the historic Courthouse on the square in\nOzark, MO. Applicants MUST be at least 62 years of age by midnight December 31, 2026;\nthe real estate MUST be located in Christian County and MUST be applicant’s primary\nresidence since at least June 29, 2026; 2026 taxes MUST be paid; Personal Property\nAssessment MUST be completed, and all applicant signatures MUST be notarized.\nWant to be alerted to emergency information in Christian County?\nDownload the Smart911 app from your app store or visit www.smart911.com to set up a user profile for your household. You will be able to select your communication preferences so public safety agencies across our county can keep you informed. It could save your life.\nFeatured Video\nCities in Christian County\nBillings\nClever\nFremont Hills\nHighlandville\nNixa\nOzark\nSparta\nVillage of Saddlebrooke\nChamber of Commerce\nNixa Chamber of Commerce\nOzark Chamber of Commerce\nRogersville Chamber of Commerce\nShow Me Christian County\nSparta Area Chamber of Commerce\nLocal News Agencies\nChristian County Headliner\nSpringfield News Leader\nSpringfield Business Journal\nQuick Links\nEmployee Portal\nDisabilities/ADA Grievance\nWebsite Accessibility\nSunshine Request Form\nChristian County Health Dept\nCopyright © 2026 · Christian County, Missouri\nLeaving Our Site\nYou are about to leave the Christian County Missouri website. Do you want to proceed?\nProceed\nCancel",
